# brev-autostop config (J516). The laptop timer stops any RUNNING Brev instance after its idle minutes.
# Live copy: ~/.config/hyprpi/brev-autostop.conf (made from this file on first use; `brev-autostop config` prints the path).
# One setting per line; # starts a comment. Changes apply at the next run (every 5 min); no restart needed.
#
#   default_idle_min N   idle minutes for every instance without its own line (also brand-new ones)
#   gpu_busy_pct N       GPU utilisation above this (any of 3 samples) counts as activity (a training run keeps its box up)
#   idle NAME N          this instance's own idle minutes
#   default_unhealthy_min N   a box stuck UNHEALTHY (or in a failed stop) this long gets one `brev stop` and an alert (45)
#   unhealthy NAME N     this instance's own UNHEALTHY limit
#   exclude NAME         never stop this instance and never probe it
#   box NAME             registered by `world X setup` (brev-autostop install NAME); uses the default
#   credit_warn_usd 50 20 10 5 1 0   (J1) dollar levels: one alert as the org's Brev credit (billingprofile
#                        remaining_credits) drops below each (0 = at or below $0), sharper each time; a level re-arms after a
#                        top-up back above it. Only warns, never stops a box. No line = off
#   credit_check_hours N how often the credit is read (3; hourly once under $20)   ·   credit_org ORG-ID   which org (default: brev's active org)
#   notify_phone on|off  alerts also as phone push notifications through ntfy.sh (J527); set it with `brev-autostop phone on`
#                        / `phone off` (on also makes the topic file ~/.config/hyprpi/brev-autostop.ntfy, 600; never put
#                        the topic here)
#
# To protect a long job, pause instead of editing: brev-autostop pause NAME 24h (or `pause NAME` until `resume NAME`).

default_idle_min 45
gpu_busy_pct 10
default_unhealthy_min 45

# Instances that must never be stopped automatically (e.g. a box someone else runs); one line each, like:
# exclude keep-me-box
